  "Question": "The arithmetic mean (average) of a set of \\(50\\) numbers is \\(38.\\) If two numbers, namely, \\(45\\) and \\(55,\\) are discarded, the mean of the remaining set of numbers is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(36.5\\)",
    "B": "\\(37\\)",
    "C": "\\(37.2\\)",
    "D": "\\(37.5\\)",
    "E": "\\(37.52\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The mean equals the total divided by the number of entries, so the original total is\n\\[\n50\\cdot38=1900.\n\\]\nDiscarding \\(45\\) and \\(55\\) removes a total of \\(100\\) and leaves \\(50-2=48\\) numbers. Their mean is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{1900-45-55}{48}=\\frac{1800}{48}=\\boxed{37.5},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
